WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.720
Shang-Chi's conception and evolution in&nbsp;
Marvel Comics has often been mired in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.880
controversy for one reason after another.&nbsp;
Here are some of the darkest moments from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.960
the legend of Shang-Chi — also known&nbsp;
as Brother Hand, the Master of Kung Fu.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.760
Those who study Shang-Chi's design from&nbsp;
the comics will no doubt notice that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.160
character came to bear more than a passing&nbsp;
resemblance to Bruce Lee in later years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.880
This was no coincidence. The character&nbsp;
was created by writer Steve Englehart and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:33.680
artist Jim Starlin in 1972 to cash in on the&nbsp;
popularity of then-novel kung fu action films.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:39.120
At first, Marvel Comics attempted to secure&nbsp;
the rights to 1972's cult classic show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.280
"Kung Fu" to adapt into a comic series.&nbsp;
When they failed to get the rights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.440
Marvel acquired the comic book rights to Sax&nbsp;
Rohmer's infamous villain Dr. Fu Manchu. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.200
Shang-Chi was initially introduced in Marvel&nbsp;
Comics as a previously unknown son of Fu Manchu.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.840
Marvels' rights to the character, however, lapsed&nbsp;
with the cancellation of "Master of Kung Fu"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:05.040
in the 80s. Later writers got around the issue&nbsp;
of not being able to use the name "Fu Manchu"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.440
by retconning the name as an alias of Shang-Chi's&nbsp;
father, whose real name is Zheng Zu. The upcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.400
live-action movie will keep to this new lore&nbsp;
by having Shang-Chi be the son of Zheng Zu.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.440
While Shang-Chi is acknowledged to be the one&nbsp;
of the most honorable heroes in Marvel Comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.560
that was not the path he was initially set&nbsp;
to follow. In the comics, Shang-Chi was born&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.760
in the Hunan province of China, where he was&nbsp;
trained in all forms of combat from a young age.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.640
At first, Shang-Chi was completely&nbsp;
obedient to his father Fu Manchu's wishes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.640
believing him to be a benevolent&nbsp;
monarch. Little did Shang-Chi know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.800
that his father was secretly one of the&nbsp;
great criminal masterminds of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.800
who had been training his son to be the&nbsp;
perfect assassin and killing machine.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:55.200
"Son, it's time for you to&nbsp;
take your place by my side."

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.000
It was only when Shang-Chi took the life of&nbsp;
Dr. James Petrie in London as part of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.040
first mission on his father's behalf that he began&nbsp;
to be troubled by what he was being asked to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.240
in the name of peace. There Shang-Chi met his&nbsp;
father's nemesis, Sir Denis Nayland Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.560
who revealed the true nature of his&nbsp;
father's evil plans for world domination.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.680
Aghast at the level of betrayal, Shang-Chi&nbsp;
turned on his father. He invaded Fu-Manchu's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.160
lair and declared they were now enemies.&nbsp;
Over the years, Shang-Chi would make good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.800
on his promise to his father by foiling his&nbsp;
plans for global domination time and again.

00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:33.280
Shang-Chi was raised to believe in the&nbsp;
utmost importance of family and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.120
clan. Unfortunately, that belief&nbsp;
became the bane of his existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.280
once he declared war on his supervillain&nbsp;
father and the rest of his criminal family.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.840
First among them was Midnight, Shang-Chi's&nbsp;
adopted brother. Although the two were not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.280
related by blood, a solid friendship had existed&nbsp;
between Midnight and Shang-Chi from an early age.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.920
That relationship came to an end once Fu&nbsp;
Manchu ordered Midnight to hunt down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.720
execute his rogue brother. Although Shang-Chi&nbsp;
pleaded with Midnight to renounce their father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.360
Shang-Chi was forced to&nbsp;
fight Midnight to the death.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.400
Just as tragic was the relationship between&nbsp;
Shang-Chi and his half-sister, Fah Lo Suee, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.680
was later given the name Zheng Bao Yu after&nbsp;
the aforementioned rights issue over Fu Manchu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.400
Although there was no love lost between Fu&nbsp;
Manchu and his daughter, her desire to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.760
her father down was far from benevolent. Fah&nbsp;
Lo Suee led her own criminal organization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.880
and her plan was to use Shang-Chi to get Fu&nbsp;
Manchu out of the way so her own gang could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.600
become the most powerful criminal organization&nbsp;
in the world. Once again, Shang-Chi was forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.600
to work against his family when he acted&nbsp;
against his sister as well as his father.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.760
"You are a product of all who came&nbsp;
before you. The legacy of your family."

00:03:44.636 --> 00:03:49.360
The tragedy of Shang-Chi's entire life has been&nbsp;
that while he is deeply committed to peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.800
it could only be achieved through&nbsp;
the death of his once-beloved father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:59.280
the supervillain Fu Manchu. Or so Shang-Chi&nbsp;
believed. To that end, the 1974 comic series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.640
"Master of Kung Fu" saw Shang-Chi track&nbsp;
down and seemingly leave Fu Manchu to die.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.040
But the passing of Fu Manchu did not&nbsp;
bring Shang-Chi the relief he imagined.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.960
After his father's death, Shang-Chi&nbsp;
embarked on a quest to save his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.600
who he imagined was being held against her will.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:21.520
After a long search, he was able to finally&nbsp;
track her down in "Master of Kung Fu #123."

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.960
But there Shang-Chi discovered that&nbsp;
his mother was no captive at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.840
but had truly loved Fu Manchu. His mother&nbsp;
renounced Shang-Chi for killing his father.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.720
The young hero was given the moniker "False&nbsp;
son" by his former comrades and mother. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.320
mission that Shang-Chi believed would&nbsp;
free the world and his mother of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.640
father's evil failed to be the moment of&nbsp;
triumph he'd so desperately hoped for.

00:04:43.814 --> 00:04:47.680
Shang-Chi discovered that letting his evil&nbsp;
father die was a more complicated act than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:54.640
he had imagined. In 1983's "Master of Kung Fu&nbsp;
#125," Shang-Chi dealt with the loss of his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.200
and his own conflicted feelings by engaging&nbsp;
in the last rites of his father's funeral.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.240
To fulfill his duties as a son, Shang-Chi&nbsp;
returned to Hunan to pay his last respects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.840
Even though he could not bear to&nbsp;
call Fu Manchu "honorable father,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.840
Shang-Chi nevertheless prayed that his&nbsp;
spirit would find peace. But his musings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:16.480
were interrupted by demons both real and&nbsp;
imagined. Shang-Chi fled to other parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.320
of China in search of something that&nbsp;
would assuage his feelings of guilt.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.400
Finally, after a twilight battle&nbsp;
against an assassin sent by his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.120
Shang-Chi drinks from his father's ceremonial cup&nbsp;
and is able to come to terms with his actions to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.160
a certain extent. But that acceptance comes&nbsp;
at a price, as Shang-Chi renounces his past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.840
as a crime fighter and settles down to&nbsp;
a simple life of farming and fishing.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:43.440
Shang-Chi's personal history has always been&nbsp;
defined by the fact that he is the only child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:49.280
of his supervillain father Fu Manchu who refused&nbsp;
to enter into a life of crime. After Shang-Chi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.600
refused his father Fu Manchu's orders&nbsp;
to work for his criminal empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.160
Moving Shadow was called upon to take&nbsp;
Shang-Chi's place at Fu Manchu's side.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.040
Moving Shadow was yet another&nbsp;
half-brother to Shang-Chi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:06.080
and raised in a similarly brutal fashion to be&nbsp;
the perfect killing weapon. But while Shang-Chi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.000
eventually came to see his father's&nbsp;
evil nature, Moving Shadow was blindly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.720
subservient and completely willing to kill&nbsp;
his half-brother at their father's behest.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:21.280
In the 2002 Marvel Max series, "Shang-Chi: Master&nbsp;
of Kung Fu," Moving Shadow came face to face with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:26.400
Shang-Chi and tried hard to kill him. No matter&nbsp;
how much Shang-Chi exhorted him to see reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.640
Moving Shadow was single-minded in his&nbsp;
desire to kill his brother. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.800
Shang-Chi emerged the victor in their&nbsp;
battle, but refused to kill Moving Shadow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:39.840
But their father had no such qualms. Dismissing&nbsp;
Moving Shadow for having failed in his mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.080
Fu Manchu personally launched a dagger&nbsp;
into his heart in front of Shang-Chi.

00:06:45.073 --> 00:06:49.440
Shang-Chi has a long history of being part of&nbsp;
superhero teams, where his even-tempered nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:55.520
and top-notch fighting skills are invariably&nbsp;
assets. The 2006 series "Heroes for Hire" saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:01.120
Shang-Chi working alongside a host of allies,&nbsp;
including the insect-powered metahuman Humbug.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:06.880
Humbug used to be Buchanan Mitty, an entomology&nbsp;
professor who turned to a life of crime to fund&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.160
his research. After constantly being foiled by&nbsp;
Spider-Man, Humbug decided to join the good guys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.680
which is how he came to be a part&nbsp;
of the super team Heroes for Hire.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:21.280
In 2006's "Heroes for Hire" series, Humbug&nbsp;
gets manipulated by the alien overlord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.840
the Brood Queen. While under the influence&nbsp;
of the Queen, Mitty ends up betraying his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:31.280
teammates to the Brood. While the team escapes the&nbsp;
Brood's prison, Shang-Chi rips Humbug's head off.

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:34.400
"Not a good time to lose one's head."

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.704
"Indeed."

00:07:36.704 --> 00:07:39.440
"That's not the way to get ahead in life."

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:40.720
"No."

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.800
One of Shang-Chi's most memorable&nbsp;
crossovers occurred with Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:49.360
in 2011's "Spider-Island" event.&nbsp;
Shang-Chi finds himself infected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.200
with something called the "spider virus,"&nbsp;
which grants him similar abilities to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.520
Spider-Man. But along with the powers&nbsp;
come a series of disturbing nightmares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:03.040
in which Shang-Chi sees himself transform into&nbsp;
a giant spider and attack innocent civilians.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.240
The vision becomes a reality in "Spider Island:&nbsp;
Deadly Hands of Kung Fu," when Shang-Chi is called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:13.840
in to help defeat the usually-heroic Bride of&nbsp;
Nine Spiders who is holding Iron Fist captive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.160
After freeing the other hero, Shang-Chi&nbsp;
discovers that Bride of Nine Spiders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:23.120
is being controlled by the god Ai Apaec, who&nbsp;
has already captured the other Immortal Weapons.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.720
While battling Ai Apaec, Shang-Chi's nightmare&nbsp;
comes to pass when the spider virus mutates him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.120
into a giant spider-like creature. The&nbsp;
spider's instincts threaten to consume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:38.160
Shang-Chi's psyche entirely. But a last-minute&nbsp;
assist from Iron Fist reminds the Master of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:42.800
Kung Fu of his true nature, and Shang-Chi&nbsp;
is able to revert back to his true form.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.840
Despite his youth, Shang-Chi's fighting&nbsp;
skills and serene nature have made him the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:53.360
go-to guy for heroes looking to brush up their&nbsp;
skills. One such hero/anti-hero was Domino,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:58.560
who sought Shang-Chi's help to become a better&nbsp;
fighter and generally a more even-tempered person.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:05.440
In 2018's "Domino #4," Shang-Chi and Domino&nbsp;
engage in an intense round of sparring. At first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:10.240
Shang-Chi is impatient with Domino's flighty&nbsp;
nature, but the two eventually grow closer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:15.440
even sharing a kiss a night club. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
things come to a head when the date is interrupted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:21.440
by Shang Chi's enemies, on the orders of Domino's&nbsp;
enemy, Topaz. Shang-Chi helps Domino recover her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.840
lost knowledge of her powers well enough&nbsp;
to take on their enemies single-handedly.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:31.600
Eventually, Domino comes face-to-face with Topaz&nbsp;
herself. Despite Shang-Chi's pleas to show mercy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.400
Domino is unable to stop herself from killing&nbsp;
her archenemy. Disappointed with his pupil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.920
Shang-Chi dismisses Domino from his tutelage, and&nbsp;
their unlikely romantic relationship also ends.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:47.200
Despite his extremely violent upbringing,&nbsp;
Shang-Chi has managed to stick to a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:52.480
pacifist path most of the time. But the Master&nbsp;
of Kung Fu has strayed from it from time to time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:57.200
like when he entered into a pact with the&nbsp;
literal Greek god of war, Ares himself.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:03.120
The conflict arose in the backup stories of&nbsp;
2019's "Sword Master" when Ares and his legion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.560
of Dragonborn soldiers got into a confrontation&nbsp;
with Shang-Chi and Sword Master. Ares wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:13.520
to get his hands on Shang-chi's ally Lin&nbsp;
Lie's mystical sword, with which the God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:18.400
of War intended to kill the kidnapper of his&nbsp;
son. Despite the misgivings of Sword Master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.760
Shang-Chi entered into a pact with Ares to aid&nbsp;
him with the sword and the retrieval of his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.840
in return for the God of War's help&nbsp;
in finding Lin Lie's missing father.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:32.720
Rather predictably, the deal soon goes south&nbsp;
as Ares, his son and Sword Master are forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:38.720
into a heated battle against Davi Naka, the Mother&nbsp;
Goddess of Madripoor. Although Shang-Chi is able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:43.920
to temporarily placate the Goddess, the actions&nbsp;
of his former teammates, the Agents of Atlas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:48.640
lead to an all-out war between the surface city&nbsp;
of Pan and the underwater city of Atlantis.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:53.360
Even after accomplishing his goal of&nbsp;
killing his father and his criminal cohort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.240
Shang-Chi was not rid of Zheng Zu's legacy.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:02.240
In 2020's "Shang-Chi" series, the Master of Kung&nbsp;
Fu discovers that Zheng Zu's spirit chose him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:07.920
be the next Supreme Commander of the Five Weapons&nbsp;
Society. At first, Shang-Chi resists the calling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.600
even after coming into contact with&nbsp;
his newly discovered half-siblings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:16.640
Brother Sabre and Sister Dagger. But eventually,&nbsp;
he agrees to team up with his siblings.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:21.840
Shang-Chi's intention is to rescue his long-lost&nbsp;
full sister, Shi-Hua, who is operating as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.560
supervillain Sister Hammer and attempting to&nbsp;
take control over the Five Weapons Society.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:31.360
Eventually, Shang-Chi comes to accept that the&nbsp;
only way to stop the infighting is to accept his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:36.480
role as the new Supreme Commander of the Five&nbsp;
Weapons. Although he vows to turn the society&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:42.080
into a force for good, his father's spirit visits&nbsp;
him upon his coronation, mockingly telling him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:48.160
"My throne suits you, my son. For you are&nbsp;
destined to become like me. Just. Like. Me."

